# A hen by a pond ringed with trees keeps her water. A seed that lands next to
# water never sprouts and never dries out, so it stays on the shore until a
# hen eats it. At a seed every 4 sunny thinks (TREE_SUN) the trees filled the
# shore within days and she died of thirst on 3 seeds of 4; at 16 she drinks
# on all 4 (tuning/foxes-hunt-more, experiment 11).
seed 7
seeds 4
pass 4
outside soil
map {
  ....................
  ....................
  ....T....T....T.....
  ....................
  ......~~~~~~~~......
  ....T.~~~~~~~~.T....
  ......~~~~~~~~...C..
  ......~~~~~~~~......
  ....T.~~~~~~~~.T....
  ......~~~~~~~~......
  ....................
  ....T....T....T.....
  ....................
  ....................
}
legend {
  . soil
  ~ water
  T tree
  C chicken
}

run 4d
expect always count only chicken >= 1      # she lives
expect died chicken of water == 0          # and her brood does not die of thirst either
expect always count seed <= 40 from 1d     # few seeds lie about (13 .. 14 at most; 126 .. 147 at 4)
